.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause
.Dd November 26, 2026
.Dt EMBER-UPDATE 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ember-update
.Nd check and install signed system and package releases
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm status | check | history
.Nm
.Cm apply
.Op Fl Fl reboot
.Nm
.Cm apply-kernel
.Ar directory
.Op Fl Fl reboot
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
selects a signed release for the installed target and OS profile.
Commands that change the system require root.
.Bl -tag -width apply-kernel
.It Cm status
Print the local status as JSON.
.It Cm history
Print up to 32 recent local update events as JSON.
.It Cm check
Check the signed channel, release, OS descriptor, and binary package catalog.
.It Cm apply
Download each selected artifact and verify its size and SHA-256.
Install the selected OS sets and package upgrades in the inactive slot.
Arm a single trial boot.
A single-root profile updates packages on its running root.
.It Cm apply-kernel
Stage the local kernel from the specified directory in the inactive slot.
The OS installer verifies the kernel files.
The resulting kernel receipt holds automatic OS changes.
Package updates remain available.
.El
.Pp
Set
.Va ember_update=YES
in
.Pa /etc/rc.conf
to check at boot and hourly.
Set
.Va ember_update_packages
and
.Va ember_update_os
to YES or NO.
.Va ember_update_channel
names the signed channel and defaults to current.
.Va ember_update_reboot
accepts ask, always, or a local interval such as 01:00-04:00.
An interval may cross midnight.
The default ask leaves the trial ready for the next restart.
.Cm apply Fl Fl reboot
requests an immediate restart.
.Pp
At startup the controller compares the running trial with the installed
receipt, checks local health, and confirms that slot.
If the kernel or health check fails, the trial watchdog returns the
device to the previous confirmed slot.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Pa /etc/ember-update-profile.json
Device target, OS set roles, and boot slot settings.
.It Pa /etc/openssl/emberbsd-release-root.pem
Installed signing trust anchor.
.It Pa /etc/ember-os-health
Local executable that must report a healthy trial within 30 seconds.
.It Pa /var/db/ember-update/state.json
Atomic status for local applications.
All users can read it.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
The
.Nm
utility exits 0 on success and exits greater than 0 on failure.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr pkg_add 1 ,
.Xr rc.conf 5 ,
.Xr certctl 8
